{"text": "Category H is for students who need the most support at school.\n\nIt is used when a serious mental illness, or behaviour that keeps happening, makes learning very hard.\n\nThe category is about the effect on learning. It is not about how smart the student is.\n\nLiam has bipolar I disorder. A psychiatrist made the diagnosis.\n\nHis mood, his sleep and his energy change a lot. Some weeks he is very low. Some weeks he is very high.\n\nThis affects his attendance, his focus and the choices he makes.\n\nThe school, his family and his doctors work from one plan.\n\nWe ask three questions. What can he already do? What is getting in the way? What support will help?\n\nOne more thing. A profile is short — one or two pages. It is for staff who help him now and then. It does not replace the IEP or the safety plan.", "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural", "audio": "category-h-slide-02.mp3", "words": [{"text": "Category", "start": 0.1, "end": 0.7, "start_char": 0, "end_char": 8}, {"text": "H", "start": 0.7125, "end": 1.1125, "start_char": 9, "end_char": 10}, {"text": "is", "start": 1.125, "end": 1.3125, "start_char": 11, "end_char": 13}, {"text": "for", "start": 1.325, "end": 1.4375, "start_char": 14, "end_char": 17}, {"text": "students", "start": 1.45, "end": 2.0125, "start_char": 18, "end_char": 26}, {"text": "who", "start": 2.025, "end": 2.1375, "start_char": 27, "end_char": 30}, {"text": "need", "start": 2.15, "end": 2.35, "start_char": 31, "end_char": 35}, {"text": "the", "start": 2.3625, "end": 2.45, "start_char": 36, "end_char": 39}, {"text": "most", "start": 2.4625, "end": 2.725, "start_char": 40, "end_char": 44}, {"text": "support", "start": 2.7375, "end": 3.2, "start_char": 45, "end_char": 52}, {"text": "at", "start": 3.2125, "end": 3.325, "start_char": 53, "end_char": 55}, {"text": "school", "start": 3.3375, "end": 3.825, "start_char": 56, "end_char": 62}, {"text": "It", "start": 4.225, "end": 4.35, "start_char": 65, "end_char": 67}, {"text": "is", "start": 4.3625,